\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Let $1\leq d<k$ and let $E\subset\mathbb R^k$ be a $d$-plane which is totally irrational, meaning its image is dense in $\mathbb R^k/\mathbb Z^k$. Choose a complementary internal subspace $F$ and projections $\pi_E,\pi_F$ along this decomposition, with $\pi_E|_{\mathbb Z^k}$ injective. A cut-and-project set from a window $W\subset F$ and a shift $s$ is
\[Y=\{\pi_E(z):z\in\mathbb Z^k+s,\ \pi_F(z)\in W\}.\]
Here $W$ is bounded, has nonempty interior, and its boundary has $(k-d)$-dimensional Lebesgue measure zero. A full-rank lattice in $E$ is generated over $\mathbb Z$ by a basis of $E$. BL equivalence means a bijection $b:Y\to L$ with $C^{-1}|y-y'|\leq|b(y)-b(y')|\leq C|y-y'|$ for a finite $C\geq1$.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is every cut-and-project set $Y$ under these hypotheses BL equivalent to a lattice in $E$? \href{https://arxiv.org/pdf/1604.06280}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must every totally irrational cut-and-project set with this regular bounded window have a bi-Lipschitz correspondence to a lattice?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{description}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, \emph{UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems}, record 6600020 (AMR-065-0020). CC BY 4.0. \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Faustin Adiceam (compiler), \emph{Open Problems and Conjectures related to the Theory of Mathematical Quasicrystals}, arXiv:1604.06280v2 (2016), Section 2.8.2, Problem 2.8.2, p. 11. \url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/1604.06280}.
\item[S3] Alan Haynes, Henna Koivusalo and James Walton, \emph{Perfectly ordered quasicrystals and the Littlewood conjecture}, arXiv:1506.05649v3 (2015), Section 2.1, pp. 6--8. \url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/1506.05649}.
